# inkling2-mini-i8.recipe -- Inkling 2 Mini with every routed expert as rotated int8: the release's
# NVFP4 experts (layers 0..19) re-quantised the way inkling2-mini.recipe already re-quantises the
# MXFP8 ones (layers 20..23). Everything else is as the release ships it. Served by arch/inkling2.
#
#   rad-convert Inkling-2-Mini -o inkling2-mini-i8.rad \
#       --recipe data/recipes/inkling2-mini-i8.recipe [--draft-model Inkling-2-Mini/mtp.safetensors]
#
#   - Why: `moe_gemm_q` at `nvfp4a8i8` has no WMMA path, while the rotated int8 form (`i8a8h`) does.
#     On one R9700 decode goes from 28.6 to 35.9 t/s and long prompts prefill about 7x faster
#     (195 t/s at 2820 tokens before, 1355 at 3220 after). A verify step runs several rows through
#     the experts, so the DSpark drafter only pays on this form: with it, 57.7 t/s on code and
#     78.6 t/s on reasoning prompts (docs/ARCHITECTURES.md, inkling2).
#   - Cost: the experts take 23.4 GiB of VRAM instead of about 15, so less is left for the cache.
#   - Quality against the NVFP4 container (rad's KL mode, full vocabulary, 25218 positions of German,
#     English and code): mean KL 0.0065 (median 0.0015, p99 0.064), top-1 agreement 97.2 %,
#     perplexity 4.737 against 4.744. The NVFP4 codes are dequantised exactly and rounded once more,
#     so this is the release's NVFP4 model to within int8 rounding, not the bf16 original.
#   - One bf16 scale per (row, 128 of K), each 128 of K rotated by the unnormalised Hadamard before
#     rounding and the 1/128 kept in the scale (`transform=fwht128`); round to nearest with a scale
#     search, no calibration data.

blk.*.e*.gu                      rtn  codes=i8 group=128 scale=bf16 transform=fwht128 clamp=sym rule=search
blk.*.e*.dn                      rtn  codes=i8 group=128 scale=bf16 transform=fwht128 clamp=sym rule=search

# The DSpark drafter, when converted with --draft-model: its derived weights stored bf16, as in
# inkling2-mini.recipe.
dspark.alpha.*                   cast dtype=bf16
dspark.markov.fold               cast dtype=bf16
dspark.markov.fold_b             cast dtype=bf16
